<LegalShell
  title="PDF tools with an architectural opinion"
  eyebrow="About"
  updated="August 27, 2026"
  description="ProjectPDF is an independent browser-first PDF toolkit built around one constraint: document bytes should not need to leave the device for ordinary PDF work."
>
  <div class="callout"><strong>The idea</strong><p>Privacy should be a property of the system, not a promise attached to an upload form. ProjectPDF therefore runs its currently live document operations in browser memory and makes exceptions visible before a person chooses a file.</p></div>

  <h2>What ProjectPDF is</h2>
  <p>It is a static web application and open project for organizing, converting, editing, securing, and signing PDFs. Its interface is built to show pages before destructive choices, explain weak or unchanged results, and connect compatible tools without asking for the same file again.</p>

  <h2>What makes it different</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Local by construction:</strong> live document tools work in the browser; completion receipts report zero document bytes sent.</li>
    <li><strong>Honest states:</strong> unfinished tools say so, conversions describe their limits, and a file that cannot safely become smaller can be returned unchanged.</li>
    <li><strong>Job-shaped workflows:</strong> playable recipes connect compatible steps using temporary, single-use browser handoffs.</li>
    <li><strong>Inspectable privacy:</strong> the privacy page is built from a source-code request audit that fails when a call is undocumented.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What it is not</h2>
  <p>ProjectPDF is not yet a mature commercial suite. It has no native apps, collaboration workspace, multilingual interface, support desk, uptime agreement, certificate-backed signing service, or cloud document store. Larger established products are a better choice when those capabilities matter more than local browser processing.</p>

  <h2>Explore</h2>
  <p><a href={`${base}/#tools`}>Browse every tool</a>, follow a <a href={`${base}/how-to/`}>connected workflow recipe</a>, read the <a href={`${base}/privacy/`}>build-audited privacy policy</a>, or inspect and report problems in the <a href="https://github.com/Bansi1701/ProjectPDF">public GitHub repository</a>.</p>
</LegalShell>
